      "message": "Good catch on the race condition during trim(40) and context re-initialization where deferred disk flushes get overwritten by re-reading the cache from disk.\n\nHowever, adding an unconditional `if (mInitialized) return;` introduces a few critical issues:\n\n1. **Unit Test Breakage \u0026 SIGSEGV (`ShaderCacheTests.cpp`)**:\n   `ShaderCacheTestUtils::terminate()` in `libs/hwui/tests/unit/ShaderCacheTests.cpp` resets `mBlobCache \u003d NULL` without resetting `mInitialized \u003d false`. With this early return:\n   - Subsequent calls to `initShaderDiskCache()` in tests (e.g. `testWriteAndRead`) return immediately, leaving `mBlobCache \u003d\u003d nullptr`.\n   - The following `load()` or `validateCache()` calls will dereference `mBlobCache` and crash with a SIGSEGV.\n   - Additionally, `ShaderCacheTests` exercises cache invalidation by calling `initShaderDiskCache` with an invalid size / identity (`size \u003d -1`). With `if (mInitialized) return;`, re-validation is bypassed and tests fail.\n\n2. **Identity \u0026 Validation Handling**:\n   `initShaderDiskCache` receives `identity` (e.g., Vulkan driver version or GLES version). If the cache is already initialized, we should verify if `mBlobCache !\u003d nullptr` and whether the identity has changed. If the identity changed or is invalid, the cache must be re-validated/cleared. If the identity matches and `mBlobCache` is already populated, we should safely skip re-reading from disk.\n\n3. **Missing Automated Unit Test**:\n   Please update `ShaderCacheTests.cpp` (`terminate()` helper and test cases) and add an automated unit test covering repeated `initShaderDiskCache` invocations while dirty cache entries are pending deferred flush.\n\n*(Generated by Jetski)*",
